  "scenes": [
    {
      "narration": "Let's draw compound growth at every interest rate on one chart. At first the lines hug. Then they explode apart.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "hook",
          "art": "crashChart",
          "props": [
            "chartUp",
            "coin"
          ],
          "lines": [
            "Compounding,",
            "every rate."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "For the first few years, one percent and ten percent look almost identical. That fools people into waiting.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "truth",
          "art": "crashChart",
          "kicker": "the trap",
          "line": "They look the same",
          "sub": "early on"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Compounding is slow at first, then shockingly fast.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-compound",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · compound interest"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Then the curves split violently, and the higher rates rocket away from the rest.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "crashChart",
          "big": "they split",
          "label": "later, violently",
          "props": [
            "chartUp",
            "fire"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The Rule of 72 tells you how many years each rate needs to double.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-rule72",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · Rule of 72"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "One penny, doubled every day for a month, ends up over five million dollars.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "crashChart",
          "big": "1¢ → $5M+",
          "label": "doubled daily for 30 days",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "fire"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "That's the raw power of the time value of money.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-tvm",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · time value of money"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s7"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The curve you're on is set by your rate, and even more by how early you start.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "Rate + time",
          "props": [
            "clock",
            "chartUp"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s8"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The cost of waiting a decade to start is enormous, and almost invisible at first.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "red",
          "line": "Waiting is costly",
          "props": [
            "clock",
            "chartDown"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s9"
    },
    {
      "narration": "And chasing a higher rate of return always adds real risk.",
